 ## App Privacy (the questionnaire)
 
-Data is collected, all of it by Google's ad SDK. These answers are from its own privacy manifest
+Data is collected by two parties: Google's ad SDK, and the game's own account and cloud save (Supabase).
+
+**The game's own account (answer these yourself; they are not in any SDK manifest):**
+
+| Data type | What it is here | Linked to the user | Used for tracking | Purposes |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Identifiers, **User ID** | The account's random id; the Game Center player id Apple gives this app (`teamPlayerID`, not a name); for a device account, a hash of a random secret | Yes | **No** | App Functionality |
+| User Content, **Gameplay Content** | The cloud save: coins, gems, record, career, the club's name, settings | Yes | **No** | App Functionality |
+
+Not collected by the game: name, email address, phone number, contacts, photos, location, purchases, browsing or
+search history, and no analytics of its own. The Game Center name and friends never reach the game's server: only
+Apple's signed id does. Requests are counted per network address for abuse limits using a hashed value kept about
+two days; that is not a listed data type and is not linked to the account.
+
+**Account deletion (guideline 5.1.1(v)):** ACCOUNT (top bar of the main menu), DELETE ACCOUNT, YES, DELETE. The
+`delete-account` edge function removes the account and every row it owns, and the app resets its local progress.
+
+**Google's ad SDK.** These answers are from its own privacy manifest
 (GoogleMobileAds.framework/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy). Xcode's privacy report (Organizer, right-click the archive,
 Generate Privacy Report) shows the same.
 
